1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
I wanted a system that could help me spot a possible freelance lead
without researching every company from a pile of tabs.

2
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:40,000
This is Global Opportunity Intelligence. Twenty-six companies are stored.
Fifty-eight signals never became a company.

3
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The high-priority count is 14, from the first scorer.
Qualified, including that set, is 21. Needs review is 5.

4
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:15,000
This run already finished. Fourteen discovered, four researched, zero qualified.
Switch says delivered. Telegram says delivered.

5
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:35,000
The targets are on the right. The shortfall is printed on purpose.
I am not going to pretend this table is a run I just started.

6
00:01:35,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Seven agents share the room. Discovery, research, technical reading,
qualification, strategy, quality assurance, and the orchestrator I talk to.

7
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The diagram is the shape. The table is stored messages,
not a claim that every agent finished this run.

8
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Switch is the room, not the model. Mattermost is where I type.

9
00:02:40,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Here is the room, and here is an exchange that already happened.
I am not going to read an old screenshot as if I typed it just now.

10
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Telegram receives the report. Two completed runs have a delivered report.
It does not email a company.

11
00:03:45,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Stitch.ai is the lead I will not pitch. The historical score is still 76.
The second reading is 70, 25, and a freelance fit of 0.

12
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Quality assurance rejected the old service line.
Approval records a decision. It does not send outreach.

13
00:04:30,000 --> 00:05:05,000
The agents do the reading. Switch is where I can see them and stop them.
The old labels are still on screen because I have not rewritten them.

14
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Global Opportunity Intelligence. Built with Switch. #HowISwitch
